<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd Allah ibn Buluggin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1073">1073</a>–1090</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn Buluggin was the last Zirid king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, ruling from 1073 to 1090 while his brother Tamim held Málaga. Caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a>, to whom he paid tribute, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>, he was deposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> in 1090 and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghmat">Aghmat</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, where he wrote a memoir that is a major source for the taifa period.</p></div>
